// static/config.flx — the numbers the whole project shares.
// Every Block that owns a subject keeps its own knobs in its fields.
//
// THE LIMITS ARE HERE, AND THEY ARE MIRRORED BY ARRAY DECLARATIONS.
// A Fluxa array is declared with a literal size — `int arr x[32]`, never
// `int arr x[config.MAX_TURTLES()]` — so a limit cannot be read from here at
// declaration time. What is here is the number every check uses; each array
// that mirrors it says so in a comment, and the two must be changed together:
//
//   MAX_TURTLES  → pool.flx (every pool), runner.flx (the a* arrays),
//                  timeline.flx (last[])
//   MAX_STEPS    → timeline.flx: taken[] is (MAX_STEPS + 1) slots per turtle,
//                  because steps are numbered from 1
//   MAX_ACTIONS  → timeline.flx (the queue)
//   MAX_STYLES   → timeline.flx (the appearance events)
//   MAX_SEGMENTS → painter.flx (segments not yet baked)
//
// Timeline.reset checks its own stride against MAX_STEPS on every run and says
// so out loud if they ever drift apart.
//
// The window size is used by main.flx in graph.init and image.new, so changing
// W and H here changes the stage. It only takes effect on a fresh run: the
// window is a `prst dyn` and its initializer is not re-run on a save.

fn W()   int { return 800 }
fn H()   int { return 600 }
fn FPS() int { return 60 }

fn MAX_TURTLES()  int { return 32 }      // turtles on the stage
// 50000, and the reason is the studio that is coming: drawing by hand spends
// steps the way nothing written by hand does. Measured when it was raised from
// 6000 — the occupancy grid in timeline.flx is turtles x steps, so it went from
// 192032 to 1600032 slots and the process from 101.4 MB to 134.5 MB resident.
// Reset stayed at 0 ms, because it is cleared only where it was written, and a
// reload does not grow it.
fn MAX_STEPS()    int { return 50000 }   // highest step number a turtle can use
fn MAX_ACTIONS()  int { return 65536 }   // movements declared, all turtles together
fn MAX_STYLES()   int { return 2048 }    // appearance changes declared
fn MAX_SEGMENTS() int { return 8192 }    // not-yet-baked segments, per save

fn SPEED()      float { return 200.0 }   // pixels per second, default
fn SIZE()       float { return 9.0 }     // turtle body radius
fn PATH_WIDTH()   int { return 2 }

fn BG_R() int { return 18 }
fn BG_G() int { return 18 }
fn BG_B() int { return 26 }
